WEBVTT

00:12:29.246 --> 00:12:33.287
you know, I I know my beliefs are correct
or I know other people are wrong.

00:12:33.829 --> 00:12:36.787
And at some point their ideas become
part of their identity.

00:12:37.579 --> 00:12:39.871
And I know even scientists struggle
with this. Right.

00:12:39.871 --> 00:12:43.162
I think at least when I was trained
as a social scientist,

00:12:43.454 --> 00:12:45.621
I was taught to be passionately
dispassionate.

00:12:46.121 --> 00:12:49.496
But I know a lot of scientists
who struggle with detachment,

00:12:49.496 --> 00:12:53.329
and you don't seem to. So how do you
keep your ideas from, I guess,

00:12:53.329 --> 00:12:54.621
becoming part of your identity?

00:12:55.121 --> 00:12:59.787
Well, I think that. I mean, this
is going to sound awful.